  "id": "field",
  "term": "field",
  "definition": "In this context, a field refers to an electric or electromagnetic influence in the brain that can affect nearby neural activity without direct synaptic contact. The packet supports this meaning specifically for ephaptic field research, where even weak fields are described as having measurable effects on brain communication and network activity.",
